 /**
  * defaultManagement.ts — D2 · network default management (master build §3 Wave 7; F2).
  *
  * The bilateral, non-custodial replacement for a CCP default waterfall. For each deteriorating
  * (pre-emptive) or defaulted seat it picks a management action, in preference order:
  *   1. SUBSTITUTE        — a gated standing substitute exists (A4 self-healing): instant
  *                          bilateral hot-swap, fully self-managed.
  *   2. RECRUIT_PROTECTION — no substitute, but third-party credit protection can be recruited
  *                          (D4): operator is NEVER the guarantor (N8).
  *   3. RE_OPTIMIZE       — neither, but the exposure can be re-netted/reduced bilaterally.
  *   4. ESCALATE          — no management path: a genuine residual gap for the operator/human.
  * A merely-watch seat that hasn't deteriorated is MONITORed. Pre-emptive (before value date)
  * is preferred to post-default — the exposure monitor (C2) feeds the deterioration signal.
